---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About | Handed the Keys"
			description="About Handed the Keys, a personal blog about working life and the stories that come with it."
		/>

		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
			}

			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />

		<main>
			<h1>About Handed the Keys</h1>

			<p>
				Handed the Keys is a personal blog about working life, the places it
				takes me, and the experiences that come with whatever happens next.
			</p>

			<p>
				It begins with my work as a substitute teacher. Every assignment is
				different. Sometimes I walk into a familiar classroom. Sometimes I
				know almost nothing about what I am walking into. Either way, one of
				the first things that often happens is simple: someone hands me the
				keys.
			</p>

			<p>
				That became the name of this blog.
			</p>

			<p>
				Being handed the keys can mean more than being trusted with a
				classroom. It can mean being trusted with a responsibility, an
				opportunity, a new role, or an entirely new chapter of working life.
			</p>

			<p>
				The posts here will primarily follow the working week: the unusual
				days, the things that went well, the things that did not, and the
				moments worth remembering. Some weeks may have more to say than
				others.
			</p>

			<p>
				Substitute teaching is where Handed the Keys begins, but it does not
				have to be where it ends.
			</p>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>